## Purpose
Prevent the validated 150 GeV Pack B benchmark builder from being mistaken for the generic interface for the next physical 2HDM scan.

## Change
Adds a short physical-point handoff note:
- current `build_model_derived.py` remains a frozen benchmark-specific builder;
- new physical points must populate all production-relevant UFO/card inputs from the canonical model row;
- `GHphiphi = -g_hH2H2` convention stays validated, but it is not assumed to be the only changing production input;
- MadGraph is rerun per new physical `point_id`;
- no general `g/g0` cross-section rescaling is used as the scan engine.

## Scope
Documentation only. No Pack A/AA/B artifact, UFO file, benchmark builder, or frozen checksum is modified. The intended next local implementation is deliberately small: a point-card writer validated first on the frozen 150 GeV benchmark.

## Scope / 范围

Complete the bounded `sizeof` / no-decay semantic cluster after merged static function relocations.

### Final implementation / 最终实现

The final branch architecture follows the mature frozen Python compiler rather than the earlier parser-fold experiment:

- Lexer classifies `sizeof` as `MINIC_TOKEN_KW_SIZEOF`;
- AST keeps a dedicated `MINIC_EXPRESSION_SIZEOF` carrying the measured type;
- supports `sizeof(type-name)` and `sizeof unary-expression`;
- suppresses array-to-pointer decay for the operand;
- preserves legacy local-array extents by materializing an array type in the unevaluated context;
- requires a bounded complete object type;
- AST verifier accepts `sizeof` only as an `unsigned long` rvalue over a valid measured type;
- cast normalization preserves the `sizeof` node without adding an evaluated operand edge;
- RV64 lowering obtains the size from target layout and emits a constant, so the operand is never executed.

This matches the mature Python `SizeOf(expr|type)` design, including its explicit unevaluated-context behavior, and avoids hard-coding RV64 object sizes into the Parser.

### Permanent regression / 永久回归

The 54th GCC/MiniC RV64 differential `sizeof_semantics` covers string literals, primitive integer/floating types, pointers, records, local arrays, and proves non-evaluation with `sizeof(bump(&side_effect))`.

Discovery Run #920 passes source inventory, clang-format 18, Debug, Release `-Werror`, ASan/UBSan, focused suites, all 54 permanent RV64/QEMU differentials, and frozen tiny-AES.

### cJSON frontier / cJSON 前沿

The unchanged pinned cJSON 1.7.19 core now crosses:

```c
length = strlen((const char*)string) + sizeof("");
```

and reaches:

```c
copy = (unsigned char*)hooks->allocate(length);
```

with exact first diagnostic:

```text
cJSON.i:175:43: error: expected ';'
```

The next missing capability is generic postfix call on a function-pointer expression / indirect-call lowering. That cluster is intentionally out of scope for this PR and will start from merged clean `main`. The intended direction follows the mature Python `Call(name, args, callee)` model: direct and indirect calls share argument handling, with RV64 `jalr` for the callee-expression path.

